<title>BRAZIL: Brazil pension funds' assets at $400 bln in 2010.</title>
<headline>Brazil pension funds' assets at $400 bln in 2010.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Assets at Brazilian pension funds will total $400 billion in the year 2010, according to estimates by Abrapp, Brazil's association of pension funds, the Gazeta Mercantil newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The estimates are based on forecasts of a 13 percent annual growth in assets in the next 15 years, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Currently, pension fund assets total about $65.6 billion.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
